'''Cardo'''<ref name="Databank" /> was a [[Force-sensitive]] [[humanoid]] [[Gender|male]] who served as a member of the [[Knights of Ren]], under the command of an individual known as [[Ren (human)|Ren]].<ref name="The Rise of Kylo Ren 1" /> Cardo, alongside [[Albrekh]], tended to the weapons and [[armor]] of the Knights.<ref name="EpIXVD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> Cardo, alongside all his fellow knights, met their end at the hands of a redeemed Ben Solo, who fought and killed them during the climactic [[Battle of Exegol]].<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Biography==
===Origins===
Sometime prior to the last [[Standard year|years]] of the [[Galactic Civil War]], Cardo became a member of the [[Knights of Ren]] and was lead by an individual known as [[Ren (human)|Ren]].<ref name="WotBH 5">[[War of the Bounty Hunters 5|''War of the Bounty Hunters'' 5]]</ref> Cardo and the knights followed the [[dark side of the Force]] and an ideology based on the [[Color|red]]-bladed [[lightsaber]] called [[Ren (lightsaber)|Ren]]. During the [[Imperial Era]], the knights remained in hiding on multiple backwater [[planet]]s to avoid the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Crimson Reign 4" />

===Serving Crimson Dawn===
====Heist at Fortress Vader====
[[File:CrimsonDawnAllies-CrimsonReign1.png|thumb|left|250px|Cardo and the knights joined Crimson Dawn in hopes of defeating the Galactic Empire.]]
Cardo and the knights were eventually recruited by [[Lady]] [[Qi'ra]] to join [[Crimson Dawn]] and help her defeat [[Darth Sidious]]&mdash;[[Dark Lord of the Sith]] and [[Galactic Emperor]]&mdash;and his Empire. At her request, the knights were tasked with infiltrating [[Fortress Vader]] in order to recover the [[Screaming Key]] from Darth Vader's vault. After Cardo and the knights arrived at the plains of Gahenn on Mustafar on the [[Night Buzzard]], they arrived at an old entrance of the fortress, which was covered by lava. After entering the fortress through the [[Sith cave]], the knights were spotted by [[Vaneé]], who called various [[Volcanic environment stormtrooper|lava troopers]] to attack them. Cardo and the knights blasted the troopers while Ren sliced through them. After reaching Vader's vault, Ren managed to recover the screaming key. Unfortunately, the knights were soon met with the arrival of [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] himself, who quickly killed one of the knights while Ren told the rest of them to run while he engaged on duel with the Sith Lord. After Ren managed to flee the duel, the knights quickly escaped the fortress with the key on their possession.<ref name="Crimson Reign 4">[[Crimson Reign 4|''Crimson Reign'' 4]]</ref>

====Mission to a hellscape====
With the key on their posesion, Qi'ra [[Mission to a dark side hellscape|sent]] the knights to a [[dark side hellscape]] where they served as protectors of [[The Archivist]], who was going there to recover an item for Crimson Dawn. After Ren activated the screaming key with the Force, Cardo and the rest were startled by the agonizing sound that the key produced, which also woke up various petrified dark side creatures that started to attack them. The knights ran through the hellscape while being chased by the creatures, Cardo and his comrades tried to blast the creatures but their blasters didn't cause any damage to them, leaving Ren to do most of the work while the knights protected The Archivist. Cardo and the knights kept fighting until the Archivist used the screaming key to unlock the item which in turn made the creatures become petrified again. Qi'ra was later informed of their success on the mission.<ref name="Crimson Reign 5">[[Crimson Reign 5|''Crimson Reign'' 5]]</ref>

====Defending the Vermillion====
[[File:CardoAndMassifShooting-BountyHunters25.jpg|thumb|right|Cardo and Massif during the fight on the Vermillion.]]
When a [[T'onga's crew|group]] of [[Bounty hunter]]s lead by [[T'onga]] infiltrated the [[Vermillion (Crimson Dawn)|Vermillion]] in order to rescue [[Cadeliah]], Cardo and the knights arrived to kill the crew.<ref name="Bounty Hunters 24">[[Bounty Hunters 24|''Bounty Hunters'' 24]]</ref>

Ren told Cardo and Massif to disarm the intruders, leaving Cardo to carry on with the orders by shooting at the bounty hunter crew. Unfortunately, one of the bounty hunters, [[Zuckuss]], took cover behind [[4-LOM]] and later shot Cardo's arm cannon, leaving him without a long-range weapon. Cardo later faced the [[Trandoshan]] [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]], while initially having the upper hand during their brawl, Cardo was grabbed by the Trandoshan and thrown into his partner [[Marinda]] while the bounty hunter crew managed to escape.<ref name="Bounty Hunters 25" />

===First Order-Resistance War===
====Skirmish on Pasaana====
Cardo and the Knights traveled with Ren to the desert world of [[Pasaana]], after learning that [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] and her allies were there. As Rey went to confront Ren. Cardo's fellow knights [[Ap'lek]] and [[Kuruk]] captured [[Chewbacca]] and brought him to some stormtroopers while Cardo and the others stood by as the Wookiee was loaded aboard a transport, alongside his belongings, and the [[Blade of Ochi of Bestoon|dagger]] he was holding. The Knights took the captive back to the ''Steadfast''.<ref name="Episode IX" />

Cardo and the other Knights also journeyed to the surface of [[Kijimi]], hunting for any sign of Rey and her allies, yet were unsuccessful in their search of the city.<ref name="Episode IX" />

====Battle of Exegol====
[[File:KyloFacesTheKnightsOfRen.png|thumb|left|250px|The now redeemed Ben Solo faces his former allies.]]
A short time after the hunt for Rey, Cardo and the other Knights of Ren were lurking in the [[Sith Citadel]] of [[Darth Sidious]] on [[Exegol]]. During the [[battle of Exegol]], Kylo Ren, now the redeemed Ben Solo, entered the Citadel to save Rey.<ref name="Episode IX" />

Before Solo could reach the [[Throne of the Sith]], Cardo and the Knights confronted their former leader. The Knights were able to swiftly overwhelm Solo in his unarmed state, forcing him to the ground and beating him. However, through the use of their [[Force-bond]], Rey was able to give Solo his [[Skywalker lightsaber|grandfather's lightsaber]]. With [[Anakin Skywalker|Anakin's]] lightsaber, Ben swiftly cut down Kuruk and Cardo before dueling the remaining Knights.<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Powers and abilities==
[[File:Cardo-TROSSeries1Base.png|thumb|right|250px|Cardo's arm cannon made him one of the few Knights that favored ranged weapons.]]
{{Quote|A Trandoshan kill me? Funny.|Cardo to Bossk|<ref name="Bounty Hunters 25" />}}
Cardo was [[Force-sensitive]] and an adept of the [[dark side of the Force]] but was untrained in [[the Force]], which resulted his powers being stunted. As a [[Knights of Ren|Knight of Ren]], Cardo displayed great martial prowess few could match,<ref name="EpIXVD" /> as shown when he was able to keep up with the Trandoshan Bossk in a brawl.<ref name="Bounty Hunters 25" />

Unlike his fellow Knights, who preferred precision based attacks, Cardo's approach left large swathes of destruction. His arm cannon packed more than enough firepower for a single soldier, effectively turning him into a walking turret. Cardo was obsessed with weapon modification, which made him the best [[armorer]] among the Knights, alongside their [[Symeong]] ally [[Albrekh]].<ref name="EpIXVD" /> Despite his great skill, Cardo was the second to fall, easily killed from a slash across the chest by his redeemed former leader, [[Ben Solo]], during the [[Battle of Exegol]].<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Equipment==
[[File:CardosBlasterPistol-MotFO.png|thumb|left|250px|Cardo's secondary weapon was a blaster pistol]]
Cardo was obsessed with weapons and weapon modifications, as such he was the most heavily armed member of the Knights of Ren. His primary weapon was a custom [[Cardo's arm cannon|arm cannon]], which incorporated three weapons into one: a rapid-fire repeating [[Laser]] [[blaster]], a [[Plasma]] bolt launcher that could fire explosive charges over 200 meters, and a [[Flamethrower]] that fired naphthex gel.<ref name="EpIXVD" />

He also carried a [[Cardo's blaster pistol|blaster pistol]] in a [[holster]] around his waist, which he primarily used as a sidearm. Finally, Cardo carried [[concussion grenade]]s strapped to his chest.<ref name="EpIXVD" />

Like the rest of the Knights, Cardo wore [[Color|black]] [[clothing]], including a [[Fire|flame]]-resistant [[Riftiaworm]]-hide coat and tri-braced [[plasteel]]-armored greaves. Cardo's [[helmet]] had the most basic design out of any of the Knights' helms, consisting of a blast furnace plate molded into a helmet shape.<ref name="EpIXVD" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Knights-of-Ren-concept-art.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Concept art of Cardo by Glyn Dillon.]]
Cardo was played by stunt performer [[Martin Wilde]] in the [[2019]] movie [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']],<ref name="Instagram">{{Instagram|username=antonsimpsontidy|url=p/B6kc4XLHjrT|name=[[Anton Simpson-Tidy]]|date=2019-12-20|quote=Now this is cool! The Knights:<br/>[[Anton Simpson-Tidy|@antonsimpsontidy]] - [[Vicrul]]<br/>[[Tom Rodgers|@tomrodgersstunts]] - [[Trudgen]]<br/>[[Ashley Beck|@ashleybeckofficial]] - [[Ushar]]<br/>[[Lukaz Leong|@lukazleong]] - [[Ap'lek|Ap'Lek]] [''sic'']<br/>[[Joe Kennard|@joe_kennard]] - [[Kuru]]<br/>@wildestunts - [[Cardo]]<br/>#adamdriver - Kylo Ren<br />Artwork by @oliverbarrett .|archiveurl=https://archive.is/VL0TE}}</ref> although the character is only listed as "Knight of Ren" in the movie's credits.<ref name="Episode IX" />

